"""spark: place work on the 4-node GB10 ring (ssh + docker, no daemon).

  spark switch [TARGET] [--detach]  change what runs: jobs, jobs-studio, jobs-studio-pair, studio-4. Preflight, unload, lease, load,
                                    verify with a GPU job per node; rolls back by itself on failure; safe to run twice
  spark profile list|apply NAME [--yes]|status      the LLM profiles (docs: profiles/README.md); a profile owns the layout
  spark layout show [SPEC]          current groups, or every valid way to cut SPEC (2x2, 2x1x1, 3x1, 1x1x1x1, 4, or 12,3,4)
  spark layout set SPEC             no-op when SPEC is the applied layout; a change goes through `spark profile apply`
  spark status                      profile, groups, role and holder of each group, live jobs
  spark claim GROUP --for TEXT      hold a group; the router gives its node only to the holder's jobs
  spark release GROUP|all           drop the hold (refused while the group has live jobs)
  spark job submit [--gpu | --blender | --cpu-only | --light] [--mem G] [--cpus N] [--once] [--shards N | --items FILE]
                   [--priority P] [--name X] [--nodes N] [--env-file-secret F] [--repo R --ref REF] [--wait] -- CMD
                                    the one way to run work: the router chooses the node from measured free memory,
                                    cores and GPU share; with no room the job waits and starts by itself
  spark job status [ID] [--all] | queue | logs ID [-f] | wait ID... | set ID --restartable | cancel ID
  spark clean [NODE...] [--yes]     finished job workspaces, old build cache, pip and uv caches; a dry run unless --yes
  spark util [--hours N] [--json]   GPU, CPU and idle share per node and for the cluster; flags idle capacity while jobs wait
  spark tick [--install]            start waiting jobs and take one utilisation sample (30 s user timer on lab)
  spark cancel ID                   ask a model job of a native profile to stop
  spark idle [--yes] [--json]      idle resident Studio model servers per node; --yes stops them (never a job's); exit 1 if one stays

Ring: spark1-spark2-spark3-spark4-spark1, direct cables. A pair must be ring neighbours.
State: ~/.local/state/spark-workloads/cluster.json, under a file lock. Per node: ~/spark/{groups,jobs,data,git}.
"""
